<%-
  envname = manifest['environment']
  summary = manifest['hiera'] || {}
-%>
<div class="page-grid page-grid-wide">
<article class="doc hiera" data-hiera data-hiera-src="hiera.json">
  <header class="doc-head">
    <p class="kind-line"><span class="kind-name">Environment</span> <span class="tag"><%= h.esc(envname) %></span></p>
    <h1 class="ident"><span class="leaf">Hiera Explorer</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">Pick a node. Each level of the hierarchy shows whether it has data for it, and opens to show what it sets. <%= summary['levels'].to_i %> levels, <%= summary['files'].to_i %> data files, <%= summary['keys'].to_i %> keys.</p>
  </header>

  <noscript><p class="callout callout-warn">This page works the lookups out in the browser, so it needs JavaScript.</p></noscript>
  <p class="callout callout-warn" data-hiera-error hidden></p>

  <section class="hiera-node" aria-label="Sample node">
    <div class="hiera-named" data-hiera-named role="group" aria-label="Sample nodes"></div>
    <div class="hiera-vars" data-hiera-vars></div>
  </section>

  <section aria-label="Hierarchy">
    <div class="hiera-find">
      <label class="hiera-find-label" for="hiera-find">Find a key</label>
      <input id="hiera-find" type="text" list="hiera-keys" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" data-hiera-find placeholder="A key, or part of one">
      <datalist id="hiera-keys"></datalist>
      <span class="hiera-find-count" data-hiera-count aria-live="polite"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="hiera-verdict" data-hiera-verdict hidden></div>
    <ol class="hiera-stack" data-hiera-stack></ol>
  </section>

  <details class="hiera-everything">
    <summary><span class="hiera-everything-title">What does this node get</span><span class="hiera-everything-count" data-hiera-all-count></span></summary>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="hiera-all">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Value</th><th scope="col">From level</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody data-hiera-all></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </details>

  <ul class="hiera-notes" data-hiera-notes hidden></ul>
  <p class="hiera-live">The values offered for a node come from the names of the data files, not from any node's facts. Encrypted values are not on this page, and nothing here was decrypted. Merges follow the <code>lookup_options</code> in this environment's data; a module's own are not read. For the live answer, on the primary: <code data-hiera-cmd></code></p>
</article>
</div>
